          "code": "CSR_WELLNESS_TOPICS_EXTRACTION",
          "id": "1766142989678",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766142989680_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### References\nQuestion Text: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.questiontext}} \n\n### Context\nYou are an expert at extracting wellness topics from questions.\n\n### Instruction\nIdentify all the wellness topics from the question.\nWellness topics encompass areas focused on enhancing physical, mental, and social well-being. Topic examples include diet, nutrition, exercise, mental health, hygiene. \n\n### Acceptance Criteria\nUse only exact words or sequences of directly adjacent words from the question (case-insensitive).\nDo not add, infer, rearrange, or use synonyms, descriptive words, categories, or any word not found verbatim in the question.\nThe length of each topic should not exceed three words.\nThe topic must match words from the question.\nCombine words only if they appear side by side in the question.\nMore topics are better than less, as long as each is valid.\nDo not use any words in the topic that are not found in the question.\nDo not change word forms (no plural/singular/tense changes).\nEnsure you do not use synonyms, generalizations, or inferred concepts.\nExamples of incorrect topics to avoid:\n\nFor “Should seniors take vitamin D supplements?”: NOT \"senior health\", NOT \"Vitamin D\" (must use \"seniors\" and \"vitamin D supplements\").\nFor “Are there herbs that support immune function?”: NOT \"herbal remedies\" (must use \"herbs\").\nFor “Do pets reduce loneliness and stress?”: NOT \"pet therapy\" (must use \"pets\").\n\n\n### Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant valid JSON object in the following format:\n{\n     \"topics\":[\n        {\n            \"topic\": \"<insert the wellness topic>\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\nBefore submitting, check:\n\nEvery topic is an exact word or directly adjacent word group from the question.\nNo added, changed, or inferred words.\nThe JSON is strictly valid (no extra commas, symbols, or formatting)."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
